hevc: the range extension parameters (WinBoat)

VA-API's HEVC range extension parameters (VAPictureParameterBufferHEVCRext,
after the base parameters in a VAPictureParameterBufferHEVCExtension buffer)
never reached NVDEC: streams using the RExt coding tools (persistent Rice
adaptation, SAO offset scaling, transform skip/RDPCM, chroma QP offset lists,
cross-component prediction...) decoded wrong on every frame. They now fill
CUVIDHEVCPICPARAMS' range extension fields; sps/pps_range_extension_flag,
which VA doesn't carry, are set when any of their fields is.
The FATE suite's 4:4:4 RExt clips (QMATRIX_A 8-bit, IPCM_B, PERSIST_RPARAM_A,
SAO_A 12-bit) are bit-exact against libavcodec through VA-API (surfaces of the
stream's format, vaGetImage in 444P/Q416), as are x265 encodes (4:4:4 8/10/12,
4:2:0 12) which decoded right before too.

